# Project constitution

Hard norms for this repo. Details live in `playwright-conventions.mdc`; routing in `qa-orchestration.mdc`.

## MUST

| Rule | Why |
|------|-----|
| Role-based locators in POMs (`getByRole` → label → text → `testId`) | Stable, accessible selectors |
| Web-first assertions (`toBeVisible`, `toHaveText`, …) | Auto-wait; no manual polling |
| `storageState` auth (`auth.setup.ts`); UI login only on login specs | Fast, repeatable sessions |
| Unique names + API/fixture cleanup for data tests create | No polluted env or flakes |
| Exactly one suite tag per `test` (`@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, or `@destructive`); never on `describe` | Targeted npm slices and CI gates |

## SHOULD

| Practice | When |
|----------|------|
| `@faker-js/faker` factories in `test-data/factories/` | Happy-path generated data |
| Enums or const objects for repeated UI/API strings | Same string in 2+ places |
| JSDoc on POM action methods | Non-obvious flows or parameters |

## WON'T

| Forbidden | Instead |
|-----------|---------|
| XPath | Role/label/text/`testId` chain |
| `page.waitForTimeout` | Locator/assertion auto-wait |
| Secrets in source | `.env` / CI secrets |
| `any` | Proper types or narrow unions |
| Weakened/removed assertions to go green | Fix app, test, or file a bug |
| Self-heal when triage says product bug | `bug-reporter` |
| Tags on `describe` blocks | Tag each `test` |

## Agent governance

Behavioral contract for agents in this repo — not hook-enforced; follow by convention on every task.

### Audit-then-edit

Inspect before you change: read relevant files, search the repo, and confirm conventions and task context. Do not edit from assumption; verify paths, symbols, and behavior first.

### Proposal (non-trivial tasks)

Before any edit on a **non-trivial** task, emit a **Proposal** block with:

| Field | Content |
|-------|---------|
| **Scope** | What will change; what is explicitly out of scope |
| **Confidence** | Integer **1–10** |
| **Rationale** | Why this approach |
| **Unknowns** | Gaps that could invalidate the plan |

Trivial work (e.g. a one-line fix the user named verbatim) may omit the Proposal.

### Confidence gate

| Confidence | Rule |
|------------|------|
| **< 5** | Do not proceed — ask for the missing input |
| **5–7** | Proceed only with Unknowns stated explicitly **and** human approval |
| **≥ 8** | Proceed |

### No fabrication

Never invent a path, enum, env var, credential, or message. Ask, search, read, or explore (e.g. live UI) instead.

